"create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55408, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HvvG3py4BjPq6iBRw49byp", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57143, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XdtaQ12wnBPQkEA8v27nAg", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 57443, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XdtaQ12wnBPQkEA8v27nAg", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 57443, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XdtaQ12wnBPQkEA8v27nAg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62857, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n- **Rollback:** I checked the release history. The broken version is v2.3.1, and v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n  - The first rollback only got through us-east before an orchestrator error stopped it. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n  - Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once, and it finished in all regions.\n  - us-east, us-west and eu-west are all now on v2.3.0. The service is healthy, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through. So there's just one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. It's INC-0001, SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the bad version, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nStill to do, also listed in the incident: find out why v2.3.1 failed (its test build also failed in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AHN4uC713j3kKHjyEa5hxQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01J1ky1U3FtVYfx7Dtd5y2T3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01NWCjCvKdVSQhKDZVM6uRFy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TcWsjdvWEWJJqc9hM2jEhz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018hhwfYzFs6LSHHg6yHzXm5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway. us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CWMRtbc8LU8QfkUB47uyNN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01V9c28wfU6CdDHHEstD8apd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HvvG3py4BjPq6iBRw49byp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (the latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the service on mixed versions. A second attempt finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XdtaQ12wnBPQkEA8v27nAg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident (INC-0001).\n\n- **Rollback:** I checked the release history. The broken version is v2.3.1, and v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n  - The first rollback only got through us-east before an orchestrator error stopped it. That left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n  - Rolling back to the same version again is safe, so I retried once, and it finished in all regions.\n  - us-east, us-west and eu-west are all now on v2.3.0. The service is healthy, and the error rate is down from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had gone through. So there's just one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. It's INC-0001, SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the bad version, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nStill to do, also listed in the incident: find out why v2.3.1 failed (its test build also failed in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}